{"source": "function Unresolved_69fe0e2d(address arg0) public payable returns (uint256) {
        require(0x04 + (msg.data.length - 0x04) - 0x04 >= 0x20);
        require(msg.sender == address(uint160(uint256(store_f))), CustomError_30cd7471());
        require(uint160(arg0) <= 0x2710, CustomError_3261c792());
        unresolved_ddca3f43 = uint256(uint160(arg0));
        emit Event_6bbc5748(uint256(uint160(arg0)));
        return unresolved_70a08231[arg0];
    }", "notes": "setFee (entrypoint_3, selector 0x69fe0e2d) reverts in the candidate while the reference succeeds: the owner check compared msg.sender to store_h, which is still zero after initialize (candidate owner() read returns 0), so the guard always failed. The owner value written by initialize/transferOwnership lives in store_f (writers Unresolved_c4d66de8, Unresolved_f2fde38b), so the guard now compares against address(uint160(uint256(store_f))). This makes setup step 2 (setFee 0x64) succeed and, with the existing write to unresolved_ddca3f43, lets the later fee read return 0x64 and getStats include the fee word, matching the reference."}
